# --- pipeline data products (regenerable; excluded on purpose) -----------------
# Downloaded genomes. Re-created byte-identically by `python run_pipeline.py`
# using the Entrez query + retrieval date recorded in data/manifest.tsv.
data/raw/

# All computed tables (guides_candidates.tsv, conservation.tsv, guides_ranked.tsv,
# summary.json, run_log.json). `results/*` rather than `results/` so that the
# single exception below can be re-included: git does not descend into an
# ignored DIRECTORY, so a negation inside one would never be consulted.
results/*

# ... with one deliberate exception. results/recommendation.md is not a regenerable
# table: it is the written reconciliation of stages 6, 7 and 8, which proposed three
# different guides on three different axes. Every number in it is reproducible from
# the TSVs above, but the selection rule and the withdrawals are an argument, and an
# argument that lives only in an ignored directory is an argument nobody can review.
!results/recommendation.md

# The manifest and fetch summary are run artifacts too. They are the
# reproducibility record for a *specific* run, so they are archived alongside a
# manuscript rather than committed to the repo, where a stale or smoke-test
# version would be actively misleading.
data/manifest.tsv
data/fetch_summary.json
data/gene_corpus_manifest.tsv

